WEBVTT

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:18.580
G-Good evening...

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.370
Oh! Sorry! Were you sleeping?

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.660
You really came.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.120
Of course I did!

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.120
I already moved so many boxes in here!

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.660
Uh, yeah. Sorry about that.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:37.950
I heard you won this room to yourself
through rock paper scissors?

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.620
But I ended up moving in...

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.830
I-I'm probably being a nuisance...

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:44.330
You're right.

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:49.000
You got the short end of the stick
living with a senior student like me!

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.120
Oh! But I was held back a year,
so we're in the same year now.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:58.410
You should stop speaking so politely,
and we can be more laid back at the dorms.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.290
Then, that's what I'll do.

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:04.700
Extraordinary skills of adaptation!

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.870
--You're in the way.
--Huh?

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:08.080
I want to leave.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.450
Oh! Sorry! Please!

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.950
"I can't win against a person
who enjoys everything so seriously."

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:57.290
I only recommended
the protein brand that I like!

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:59.120
Y-Yeah.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:02.290
Then, do you know what he said?

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:05.410
"Are you saying my bodybuilding is sloppy?"

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:06.830
That's what he said!

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:11.160
Let me repeat myself. I only
recommended the protein brand I like!

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:15.870
Would a normal person think that
I was insulting their body with just that?!

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.290
They wouldn't...

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:19.790
That's what I thought!

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:22.080
I was just trying to be friendly...

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:24.370
Now our dorm room is silent!

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.250
No conversation!

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:26.910
I can't stand it!

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.410
That sounds terrible...

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:32.160
He didn't hate me this much in high school...

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.040
No, wait.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.370
Maybe I just didn't notice?

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:40.250
Maybe he's always hated me?!

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:42.000
I wonder...

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.500
Hey, Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>!

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.370
Aren't your responses a little shallow?!

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.870
Are you really listening to me?

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:50.330
Listen, Natsusa-<i>kun</i>.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:54.950
As you can see, I'm currently
dealing with something...

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:57.370
Can we talk about this later?

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:00.450
Hey!

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:01.160
"This is dangerous. Do not imitate."
Hey!

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:05.580
"This is dangerous. Do not imitate."
To begin with, when are you going
to become a starting member again?

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:08.410
You've already been on
the B Team for three weeks.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:11.580
Natsusa! Your misdirected anger
is really dangerous right now!

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:15.540
Seiichirou! Don't just stand there, back me up!

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:17.750
--Natsu...
--Whoa!

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:24.000
We've been winning without Ibuki-<i>san</i>.
He doesn't have to be there. Don't worry.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:24.950
No, no, no, no!

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.700
You're totally backing me up in the wrong way!

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.200
If we were a band, we would
have disbanded just now!

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:32.250
At the level, we'd never
get back together again!

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.620
So?

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:40.500
Well, praise me!

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.580
I became a member of the team?

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:46.200
Isn't being the number 10
stand-off your true calling?

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:51.120
Do you really think you can
fully shine as the number 20?

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:54.120
Don't get so excited receiving any old number.

00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:59.160
That ain't good.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:01.660
Those words were way too harsh.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:03.910
Natsusa was in the wrong just now...

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:06.870
Senpai, please cheer up!

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:22.540
"Fourth Year College Student" "Atomu Gotou"
"Number 17, Reserve"
Sousuke, have you broken in
that mouthpiece of yours?

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:25.290
No, not yet.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:29.080
You'll be fine. You shouldn't
get hit that much today.

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:31.080
We should win with a pretty big gap.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:33.910
True. But I'm not feeling great today.

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:36.040
I was up late last night.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:38.790
What the hell were you doing before a match?

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:41.120
I'm gonna take a little nap.

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:43.870
Natsusa, wake me up when we get there.

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:45.910
Right here.

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.410
Huh?

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:52.040
You do realize there is a proper guideline
marking the space of a single seat, right?

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.540
That line is right here.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:06:00.950
As you can see, the three of you are
currently taking up 1.5 seats per person.

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:04.000
The three of you know that you are larger
than the average person, right?

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.290
How can you sit so casually, knowing that?

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:10.160
At the very least, shouldn't you show
some effort and try to fit in a single space?

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:13.790
Even if it's impossible for you, it would
change the feelings of those around you.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:18.500
You are all slouching, leaning,
and spreading out your legs

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.080
just like an insensitive old man.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:20.830
"They fall over on you when they fall asleep."
just like an insensitive old man.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:21.910
"They fall over on you when they fall asleep."
"I'd forgive a cute girl. lolol"
I mean, what is up with that?
Do their legs automatically spread open

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:23.370
"I'd forgive a cute girl. lolol"
"Don't drool"
every time they sit down?

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:24.410
"No. Makeup is a nuisance, too."
"Seriously annoying."
every time they sit down?

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:25.660
"No. Makeup is a nuisance, too."
"Seriously annoying."
Before complaining about things like makeup,

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:28.040
"Don't fill up a seat with your things. lololol"
"Don't eat on the train."
don't you think they should consider

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:31.000
"*This is only his personal opinion."
how annoying they are themselves?

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.500
Sorry...

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:36.410
Hey, Seiichirou.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:38.660
Why is Natsusa in such a bad mood?

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:41.370
Huh? Is he in a bad mood?

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:44.950
That's exactly why you can stay
with Natsusa all the time...

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:49.950
Natsu-<i>senpai </i>seems like such a kind senior.
Does he ever get mad at you, Yuu?

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:52.450
He's never gotten mad at me.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:56.040
But he's always furious with Ibuki-<i>san</i>.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:57.790
As well as the other seniors.

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:01.950
Natsu-<i>senpai </i>never got mad
at his juniors in high school, either.

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:03.580
Right, Yasunari?

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:07.750
Hey, Yasunari!

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:09.080
"Doushisha University Wing
Natsusa Yuzuki"

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:11.410
What are you doing?!

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.000
S-Sorry...

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.910
What kind of attitude is that?

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:17.450
Does he think it's cool or something?

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.160
Hey, Kotori!

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:22.700
Please stop!

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.410
Stop it.

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:29.790
Come on, Kotori!

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:37.580
Looks like Taisei will definitely
be the captain of his generation.

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:41.790
It'll be the first time someone from our
high school becomes a Doushisha captain.

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:43.870
It's still too early to tell, Mako-<i>san</i>.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:48.700
The team was particularly strong the year
you were captain back in high school.

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:54.080
I was happier when you
were captain, Mako-<i>san</i>.

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:56.540
Taisei's passion was suffocating
when he was captain.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:58.120
Hey.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:03.080
Well, I was only captain through
the process of elimination.

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:10.870
Natsusa Yuzuki!

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:16.750
Wow! The real thing!

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:20.540
Nice to meet you!
My name is Ryuusei Hiyoshi!

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:22.160
N-Nice to meet you.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:24.750
"Isui University First Year College Student"
"Ryuusei Hiyoshi" "Number 14, Right Wing"
I'm a fan! Please shake my hand!

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:26.870
Huh? Oh...

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:34.410
I originally did dance, but I started rugby
after seeing how cool you were!

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.750
Huh? Really?

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:40.790
Yes! I read a magazine interview that said
you did dance when you were little

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:43.870
and that it may have
affected your step work!

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:46.700
That's why I thought maybe
I would be able to do rugby, too!

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:48.660
I-Is that so?

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:52.040
I didn't really take dance lessons...

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:55.330
It was more like I imitated
my cousin's dancing...

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:57.950
This is so moving!

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:00.040
Hey, Ryuusei! What are you doing?

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:03.790
Oh! Senpai! Please look!
It's Natsusa Yuzuki!

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:05.500
I got it, so stop.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:07.620
And it's rude of you to say
his name like like that.

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:09.700
Oh, shoot!

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:14.700
A lot of famous people are referred to
without adding a -<i>san </i>to their name...

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:17.830
It was something like that. I'm sorry!

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:20.500
No way! I'm not famous or anything...

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:22.620
I'm sorry. He's an idiot.

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.660
No, no! Not at all!

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.160
We look forward to the match today.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:28.250
Hey, let's go!

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:29.160
Wait!

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:31.290
Oh, I bought some colored paper!

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:33.580
Please give me your autograph later!

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:36.330
Listen.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:38.870
This isn't a match we can lose.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.700
Don't underestimate our opponents.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:45.500
The supervisor, coach, and players have changed.
They're different from last year.

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:48.000
Don't let them disrupt our pace.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.910
We're going to play cautiously from the start.

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:53.000
--Got it?
--Yes!

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.200
--Who are we?
--Doushisha!

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:57.950
"Kansai University Rugby A League
Doushisha University
VS
Isui University"

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:00.250
"Doushisha University"    "Isui University"

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:08.700
What a beautiful line.

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.660
Yes! Very much so!

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:16.080
Looks like there's no place for a reserve
like you to shine, Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>.

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:21.330
"Doushisha University"                  "Isui University"

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:31.450
"Doushisha University"        "Isui University"

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:37.120
Come to think of it, has Seiichirou-<i>san</i>
ever missed a conversion goal?

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:39.540
I've never seen him miss...

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:42.950
No, he seriously doesn't miss.

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:46.790
Of course, up until his second year of
high school, he would sometimes miss.

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:50.870
But the more he practices, the less he misses.

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:55.160
That's because Sei doesn't get nervous.

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:56.870
He doesn't get nervous?

00:10:56.870 --> 00:11:00.700
Right. With conversions,
once you master the technique,

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:03.040
your mental strength becomes the main hurdle.

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:05.250
He's strong because he
never budges under stress.

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:08.700
I see. He's an amazing person.

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:11.910
Yeah! He's a best friend to be proud of!

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:20.000
He's running from a place like that?

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:28.700
This step work...

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:30.450
Stop right there!

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:35.500
Aw, guess it wasn't good enough!

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:38.660
Huh? That step work...

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:42.620
Yasunari looks pretty shaken.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:52.660
Shit!

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:03.700
You!

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:11.200
I've got to make it!

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:24.080
Yay!

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:27.040
What was that just now?

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:28.580
Calm down.

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:32.120
He's not Natsu.

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:40.200
"Doushisha University"          "Isui University"

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:44.160
Natsusa, he's a pretty serious fan.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:48.950
Everything, from his step work
to his running, is just like mine...

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.080
Tsuru, calm down.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:58.040
You have the skills for this.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.410
Yes.

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:02.830
Don't talk to him.

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:06.410
I won't. I'm not that oblivious.

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:09.290
Yuu, please go ice Yasunari down.

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:10.620
Yes!

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.950
"Doushisha University"       "Isui University"

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:37.910
Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>, we should tape you up soon.

00:13:38.950 --> 00:13:41.830
Natsusa-<i>san</i>, you are really good at taping!

00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:44.620
It's pretty hard to do
taping for other people...

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:47.040
I've been doing it since high school.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:50.410
In the beginning, I did it because
Sei couldn't do it himself.

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:54.080
Then, Ibuki-<i>senpai </i>had
the nerve to ask me to do his...

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:57.700
Is it your goal to say something mean
to me at least once per conversation topic?

00:13:57.700 --> 00:14:01.370
No. I was just talking about
how spoiled you are.

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:08.250
Now that I'm used to Natsusa's taping,
I can't do my best without it.

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:11.910
That's why I live with the
complaints and have him do it.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:15.830
Well, stable taping helps
to stabilize your mentality!

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:17.620
Oh! Wise words!

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:20.040
There, I'm done.

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:24.330
Okay. Feels good.

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:25.950
I'll go warm up.

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:27.910
What was that just now?

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:30.290
That little piece you cut off...

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:33.450
Oh, it's a charm.

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:36.250
In hopes that he comes back
without any injuries.

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:38.580
I've been doing it since high school.

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:44.830
Once, when Ibuki-<i>senpai </i>just happened
to have a piece of taping there,

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:49.410
he got hit by a really high tackle,
but wasn't hurt at all.

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:55.500
He really thinks the reason he hasn't
gotten seriously hurt is that charm.

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:57.370
That's pretty unexpected.

00:14:57.370 --> 00:15:00.790
You think? That person is pretty simple.

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:05.290
His mental state is unstable
without any jinx or routines.

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:15.080
Crap!

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:16.910
All right!

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:19.750
Try!

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:32.080
"Doushisha University"        "Isui University"

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:33.200
"Doushisha University"        "Isui University"
Doushisha University.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.950
"Doushisha University"        "Isui University"
Number 10 out. Number 20 in.

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:38.790
Number 5 out. Number 19 in.

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:42.750
Number 14 out. Number 23 in.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:44.540
Take care of things.

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:45.910
Yes.

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:56.290
Welcome home, Ibuki.

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:58.040
You're finally back.

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:00.330
You're the same as usual.

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:04.950
Your passing sucks. Your step work is average.
And you aren't reading the game.

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:10.700
That's Ibuki's job. Hurry up and
support me so I can stand out!

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:15.040
I really think your personality
doesn't fit rugby at all...

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:17.700
I can just run without thinking, right?

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:19.830
My sweetheart?

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:23.040
Do what you want, darling.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:28.620
We're going to have a new member
join us just for the summer.

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:30.750
His name is Ibuki Ueoka.

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:34.290
He's from the Kyushu rugby school.

00:16:34.290 --> 00:16:36.200
Please take care of me.

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:48.500
What the hell! Why isn't there any
proper support! You're all useless!

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:51.950
Why are you pissed?
The useless one here is you.

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:52.950
What?

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:57.450
I mean, it looks like all you can do
is hold the ball and run.

00:16:57.450 --> 00:17:02.450
So what? I'm doing something
you Japanese can't do.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:03.870
Right.

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:07.620
I'll support you.

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:10.250
Wh-What do you mean?

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:12.040
Exactly what I said.

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:16.040
I've figured out how narrow
your vision is during the first half.

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:20.950
I'll make the useless you become useful.

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:24.000
Do you trust me?

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:28.870
Shit! Again!

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:39.830
Yamato Nadeshiko...

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:42.000
Hey, you!

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:47.950
Play on the same team with me!
I've never seen a Yamato Nadeshiko like you!

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:52.200
Do you know what Yamato Nadeshiko means?

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:56.450
I do! They are Japanese people
who support a man!

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:59.250
Support me for life!

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:05.250
Well, whatever. If you want my support,
you're going to have to join my team.

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:06.500
Me?!

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:08.080
Of course.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:13.450
If you don't have that kind of guts,
you'll never catch a Yamato Nadeshiko,

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:15.160
darling.

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:22.620
Shit!

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.370
What?!

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:39.330
Great, Ibuki.

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:43.790
As I thought, I can only play
freely when you're here.

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:48.000
Will you marry me?

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:50.870
In Japanese, please?

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:53.040
I was able to run without a mark...

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:56.290
Why didn't Ueoka-<i>san </i>throw me a pass?

00:18:56.290 --> 00:18:58.000
I've got to do something...

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:00.830
I need to regain his trust...

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:23.330
Ibuki!

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:25.660
I know! You're so noisy!

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:33.500
It's no use! He won't stop!

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:34.700
Shit!

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:39.830
All right! Lucky!

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:02.200
Seiichirou! I thought maybe
I read the flow wrong for a second!

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:04.700
Run forward a little faster!

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:07.080
Even though I didn't rush, I made it in time.

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:08.950
That's not the problem here!

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:11.370
It brings down the tension of the match!

00:20:11.370 --> 00:20:12.750
Ibuki!

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:14.830
And your tension is way too high!

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:19.910
Amazing... Ibuki-<i>san </i>can really do everything!

00:20:19.910 --> 00:20:21.910
Isn't he getting a little cocky?

00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:25.290
I-Isn't it fine to g-get a little cocky
every once in a while?!

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:28.750
If we make the next
conversion kick, we'll be tied!

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:31.620
Y-You're right. Sorry...

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:47.580
"Doushisha University"        "Isui University"

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:50.500
Oh, thank goodness.

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:53.080
The wind is pretty strong today.

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:56.080
Oh. Yeah...

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:57.580
That's weird...

00:20:57.580 --> 00:21:01.250
The wind doesn't matter for Sei...

00:21:01.250 --> 00:21:02.830
Okay. This is the starting point.

00:21:02.830 --> 00:21:04.120
Move forward with caution!

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:05.410
Yes!

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:09.200
Shit! Shit! Shit!

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:10.870
I have to do something!

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:15.450
If I don't, I'll lose against him!

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:20.160
This isn't funny! I won't let you pass!

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:21.450
You idiot!

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:28.290
Captain.

00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:33.910
That tackle was considered foul play.
Yellow card. Understood?

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:35.290
Yes.

00:21:36.410 --> 00:21:37.790
Tsuru.

00:21:44.330 --> 00:21:48.160
We lost a player at a time like this...

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:51.200
And that opposing number 14...

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:57.830
"Doushisha University"      "Isui University"

00:21:57.830 --> 00:21:59.910
"Doushisha University"      "Isui University"
No side.

00:21:59.910 --> 00:22:02.080
We did it!

00:23:41.950 --> 00:23:43.540
"Regression is also evolution."
This is Yasunari Tsuru.

00:23:43.540 --> 00:23:45.910
"Regression is also evolution."
The next number is,
"Regression is also evolution."

00:23:45.910 --> 00:23:46.910
"Regression is also evolution."
Please watch.
